  "stateNote": "In a large bowl, beat one egg white (keep the yolk separate) and a little water into a foam (careful, grease or fat prevents foam from forming, and you end up with an unappetizing runny egg-white). To stabilize the foam add the juice of one lemon. Continue to whisk as you add the egg yolk. This is called \"avgolemono\" (egg and lemon) and is used to thicken soups (instead of heavy cream).",
